00:00:55.722 --> 00:01:01.348
And to have that as part of my life, especially being where I am and doing what I do.

00:01:01.348 --> 00:01:05.677
I'm not exactly like surrounded by lots of other Japanese people.

00:01:05.677 --> 00:01:12.270
So it's really on me to like make this environment for myself in which I can connect to my history.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.826
And before I get into the how I wanted to also talk about
why it's really important to me,

00:01:16.826 --> 00:01:17.326
I think growing up, it was kind of like a sense of like legitimacy, like, the closer I was to staying in touch with the Motherland,

00:01:17.326 --> 00:01:24.870
the more legit of a Japanese person that I was.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:30.990
And that's definitely faded
some more because I'm kind of like I am whoever I want to be.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.490
And I can take all the different parts to myself,
legitimate or not, like, I'm just me.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:37.290
But I've since realized that it's important for me to stay connected, because being Japanese is a huge part of who I am.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:52.440
Like, I look Japanese, like I'm 100%, like ethnically Japanese, I
was super Japanese name, I grew up with Japanese parents

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:59.430
speaking Japanese. So it's just Yeah, it's a core part of my
identity. And moving forward, I kind of want it to continue

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:05.610
being a part of my life, because I like that side of me. And
I think it's cool that I get to experience the world in my

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:10.950
life through this other culture as well. So yeah, I've just
