brings us to different neighborhoods that maybe we wouldn't

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:34.650
have tried before. So yeah, coffee, experiencing different
food experiencing different neighborhoods, kind of seeing

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:42.480
Japan for what it is at the current moment and experiencing
it as much as possible through like, current eyes, I guess.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:50.010
Because one of the things is like, once your family I feel
like immigrates outside of the Motherland, then some of the

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:56.670
values and stuff that they bring with them can tend to be
like a snapshot of the last time they live there. And so I

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:03.930
know that like, you know, Japan is changing, like everywhere
else. And trying to understand how it's changing how the

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:09.390
culture is changing, what are the sentiments of the people
there, I think is really interesting. Like I like thinking

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:17.220
about that stuff. So whenever I go trying to kind of get
that sense, and talking to locals, and having them always

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:24.240
surprised that I not only speak Japanese, but also speak
kansai-ben can be kind of a fun experience. So yeah, I just

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:30.090
I can't wait for the pandemic to end because then I'm going
to go back there and enjoy. Like literally before the

